#!/bin/sh
# security-audit: read-only daily security report. Takes no arguments, changes nothing
# (rkhunter appends to its own log). Design: REQUEST-atlas-to-otto-2026-10-31-daily-security-audit.md
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
LC_ALL=C
export PATH LC_ALL
[ "$#" -eq 0 ] || { echo "usage: security-audit (no arguments)" >&2; exit 2; }
[ "$(id -u)" -eq 0 ] || { echo "run as root: sudo -n /usr/local/bin/security-audit" >&2; exit 2; }
h() { printf '\n## %s\n' "$1"; }

echo "# security-audit $(hostname) $(date -u '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M UTC')"
echo "boot: $(uptime -s)   load: $(cut -d' ' -f1-3 /proc/loadavg)"
df -h / | tail -1 | awk '{print "disk /: " $3 " used, " $4 " free (" $5 ")"}'
free -h | awk '/^Mem:/ {print "ram: " $7 " available of " $2} /^Swap:/ {print "swap: " $2}'

h "1. Logins (last 24 h)"
J=$(journalctl -u ssh --since -24h --no-pager -o cat 2>/dev/null)
echo "### accepted (count, user, ip, key)"
echo "$J" | grep -E '^Accepted ' | sed -E 's/ port [0-9]+//' | sort | uniq -c
echo "### failed attempts: $(echo "$J" | grep -cE 'Failed |Invalid user|Connection closed by authenticating user')"
echo "### fail2ban sshd"
fail2ban-client status sshd 2>&1 | grep -E 'Currently|Total|Banned IP'

h "2. Who can get in"
for d in /root /home/*; do
  f="$d/.ssh/authorized_keys"
  [ -f "$f" ] && { echo "### $f"; ssh-keygen -lf "$f" 2>&1; }
done
echo "### users with a login shell"
awk -F: '$7 !~ /(nologin|false|sync|halt|shutdown)$/ {print $1 " uid=" $3 " " $7}' /etc/passwd
echo "### sudo group: $(getent group sudo | cut -d: -f4)"
echo "### sudoers files"
sha256sum /etc/sudoers /etc/sudoers.d/* 2>/dev/null

h "3. Config integrity"
sha256sum /etc/ssh/sshd_config /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/* /etc/fail2ban/jail.local /etc/ufw/user.rules /etc/ufw/user6.rules 2>&1
echo "### nginx tree"
find /etc/nginx -type f | sort | xargs sha256sum
echo "### sshd effective"
sshd -T 2>/dev/null | grep -E '^(permitrootlogin|passwordauthentication|kbdinteractiveauthentication|pubkeyauthentication) '
echo "### ufw"
ufw status verbose

h "4. What is running"
echo "### listening (proto, address, process)"
ss -Hltnup | awk '{print $1, $5, $7}' | sed -E 's/,pid=[0-9]+,fd=[0-9]+//g' | sort -u
echo "### top 10 by cpu"
ps -eo user,pcpu,pmem,comm --sort=-pcpu | head -11
echo "### processes running from /tmp, /dev/shm, /var/tmp, or a deleted binary"
for p in /proc/[0-9]*; do
  e=$(readlink "$p/exe" 2>/dev/null) || continue
  case "$e" in /tmp/*|/dev/shm/*|/var/tmp/*|*" (deleted)") echo "pid ${p#/proc/}: $e";; esac
done
echo "(end of list)"
echo "### enabled systemd units"
systemctl list-unit-files --state=enabled --no-legend | awk '{print $1}'
echo "### crontabs"
for u in $(cut -d: -f1 /etc/passwd); do
  c=$(crontab -l -u "$u" 2>/dev/null) && { echo "#### user $u"; echo "$c"; }
done
find /etc/crontab /etc/cron.d /etc/cron.hourly /etc/cron.daily /etc/cron.weekly /etc/cron.monthly -type f 2>/dev/null | sort | xargs sha256sum

h "5. Files changed in the last 24 h (names only)"
for d in /etc /usr/local/bin /srv; do [ -d "$d" ] && find "$d" -xdev -type f -mtime -1 2>/dev/null; done | sort

h "6. Rootkit (rkhunter, warnings only)"
R=$(nice -n 19 rkhunter --check --sk --rwo --nocolors 2>&1); rc=$?
echo "${R:-no warnings}"
echo "(rkhunter exit $rc: 0 = clean)"

h "7. Virus (ClamAV, infected files only)"
echo "engine/signatures: $(clamscan --version 2>/dev/null)"
T=""; for d in /home /srv /tmp /var/tmp /etc; do [ -d "$d" ] && T="$T $d"; done
C=$(nice -n 19 ionice -c3 clamscan -r -i --no-summary $T 2>&1); rc=$?
echo "${C:-no infected files}"
echo "(clamscan exit $rc: 0 = clean, 1 = infected found, 2 = error)"

h "8. Patching"
U=$(apt list --upgradable 2>/dev/null | grep -i -- '-security')
echo "${U:-no pending security updates}"
if [ -f /var/run/reboot-required ]; then
  echo "REBOOT REQUIRED by: $(tr '\n' ' ' < /var/run/reboot-required.pkgs 2>/dev/null)"
else
  echo "no reboot required"
fi
